(text "Sheet 4: gate drivers, current sense and fault comparators" (at 25.4 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid 22adbe58-1b97-5ecd-8f43-587f261aa58e))
(text "Fault thresholds (dividers from VREF25 = 2.500 V, U10):\nREF_A 0.114 V = 3.4 A in R13 (boost switch)\nREF_B 1.92 V = 43.2 V on VLED\nREF_C 1.38 V = 6.9 A charge current\nREF_D 1.49 V = 15.0 V battery\nU10 current: about 0.24 mA (R48 0.83 mA minus 0.59 mA in the dividers)" (at 284.48 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 42702aee-6039-5ea8-aaa6-b59dfa7df079))
(text "U2 LM2901: open-collector outputs wired together on FLT (U1 pin 24, active low, latched, 1 us filter). Signal on -, threshold on +, so a fault pulls FLT low." (at 25.4 185.42 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 41e36d22-84ee-5edd-b5c8-a46097f408c7))
(text "Notes\n- R29, R30, R33: PWM pins go high-impedance on a FLT fault; these keep the drivers off (SD low = both FETs off).\n- U4 IR2104: IN = PWM0 (high = Q3 on, low = Q4 on), SD = P0.1 as GPIO. Dead time (about 520 ns) is set inside U4.\n   It cannot hold Q4 off while Q3 switches: below about 0.2 A charge current, firmware stops switching with SD.\n- U4 VS pin is SW_C (sheet 1). D16 (ultrafast, >=100 V) and C36 (100 nF) form the bootstrap supply.\n- U7 split outputs: R34 sets turn-on speed, R35 turn-off.\n- U5: charge current 5.8 A -> 1.16 V, 7 A -> 1.40 V.  U6: LED current 0.565 A -> 1.13 V.\n- U6 IN- (pin 4) must be Kelvin-routed to the ground pad of R14, not to the nearest ground." (at 25.4 233.68 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 3395c1c9-a074-574c-8190-f46111783009))
)
